From 3b974eab305b1a7f23b2d4b22091b2806abce4fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:32:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(app): enter a cross hole where its own line meets the
 stock

The cross drill read the setup stock by its largest vertex radius, so a
box counted at its corner circle: a 60x60 box put the mouth at r42.4
although the face is at r30 (air drilling, extra Auto pecks), and the
#84 reach check measured depth from that over-far mouth - a 30 mm hole
from the face of a 44 mm square bar read 39.1 mm and a 35 mm flute was
falsely refused.

Each hole's mouth is now where the drill's body (a square tube of
half-width d/2 about the hole's line, a superset of the round drill)
first meets the stock mesh, in the spindle frame; the shank's #84
reach is read the same way at its half-width. A round bar keeps the
circumscribed reading bit for bit: the mesh replaces it only when the
crossing stands more than raw*(1-cos(pi/16)) inside it (a flat face,
not a tessellated round's chords), and a tube meeting no facet falls
back to it. rapids_clear judges a rapid along a hole's line against
that per-line entry; every other rapid and the kernel's hop/clearance
planes still stand off the circumscribed radius, so station-change
hops clear the box corners.

Fixes #85

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
