From 9a095b72db3d978434ae47ecca7f7ffa912676bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:48:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(app): read a cross hole's entry at the true round,
 part included

Review fixes for the #85 per-line entry.

The flat-face band was measured against the global raw radius, so a
round well inside it (a stepped bar's d40 section under a d60 step, an
off-axis cylinder stock, a round boss) was read at its chords on
grazing off-centre lines: the mouth inside metal and the #84 reach
short. Each stock facet is now read as its sagitta slab, thickened by
(h/2) tan(theta/2) from the dihedral to its edge neighbours; dihedrals
above 45 degrees are real edges, so box faces and hex flats stay exact
and a round bar's chain is bit for bit (fingerprint re-checked on the
pre-#85 parent).

The per-line entry also reads the part's facets beside the stock's, so
a part poking out of a box face still bounds the mouth and the
along-line rapids. The refusal message regains its line continuations,
cross_entry is a plain module of operation, and the shank branch of the
along-line proof is pinned on box stock.

Refs #85

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
